module waed-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Eastern District of Washington's own criminal periods, counted under
// the criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). The rules
// are subject to any order of the presiding judge in an individual case
// (LCrR 1(a)). No trigger carries a service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three
// added days follow the manner of service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay with the Federal Rules and are
// only named here: objections to a magistrate judge's report and
// recommendation on a felony plea are filed within fourteen (14) days
// after its service (LCrR 11(i)), FRCrimP 59(b)(2)'s period.
//
// A period in hours stays in a note, because language version 1 lowers no
// hour deadline: when the initial appearance after a warrantless arrest
// will not or is likely not to be held within forty-eight (48) hours, a
// complaint and affidavit are presented to the Magistrate Judge within
// forty-eight (48) hours after the arrest (LCrR 5(b)(1)).
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: a copy of
// a preliminary hearing recording will "whenever possible" be provided
// within five (5) days of the request (LCrR 5.1(g)(1)); an expedited
// motion sets a hearing not less than seven (7) days after its filing
// (LCrR 12(c)(3)), a floor on the setting; a response to a reconsideration
// motion is filed only on the court's request, which sets its time (LCrR
// 12(c)(5)); a motion to transfer under FRCrimP 21 is made within the time
// for pretrial motions (LCrR 21(d)); the LCivR 7.1 response and reply
// periods include FRCrimP 45(c)'s three days regardless of the method of
// service (LCrR 45).
//
// The earlier E.D. Wash. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// belong to lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is
// vendored.
/// A motion for reconsideration: limited to five (5) pages (E.D. Wash.
/// LCrR 12(c)(5)).
limit reconsideration-motion {
  pages <= 5 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 12(c)"
} cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 12(c)"

/// Written objections to a magistrate judge's plea report and
/// recommendation are served (E.D. Wash. LCrR 11(i)).
event PleaObjectionsServed()
/// A motion for reconsideration is filed (E.D. Wash. LCrR 12(c)(5)).
event ReconsiderationMotionFiled() paper reconsideration-motion
/// The defendant is arraigned (E.D. Wash. LCrR 16(a)).
event Arraigned()
/// Trial is set (E.D. Wash. LCrR 16, 23(d), 24(a), 30(a)).
event TrialScheduled()
/// A notice of appeal from a magistrate judge's order or judgment is filed
/// (E.D. Wash. LCrR 58(g)(2)(E)).
event MagistrateAppealNoticed()
/// The appellant's brief is filed and served (E.D. Wash. LCrR
/// 58(g)(2)(E)).
event AppellantBriefServed()
/// The appellee's responsive brief is filed and served (E.D. Wash. LCrR
/// 58(g)(2)(E)).
event AppelleeBriefServed()

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 11(i): a party opposing objections to the plea report
/// and recommendation files and serves a written response within seven (7)
/// days thereafter.
deadline plea-objection-response: 7.days after PleaObjectionsServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 11(i)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 16(a): absent notice to the contrary, at arraignment or
/// within fourteen (14) days thereafter the government makes its Rule 16(a),
/// interception, search warrant, warrantless seizure, identification and
/// Brady disclosures.
deadline government-disclosure: 14.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 16(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 16(a)(7)-(9): no later than twenty-eight (28) days
/// before trial, the government provides Henthorn information, its Rule
/// 404(b) summary and its Rule 609 convictions list.
deadline government-pretrial-disclosure: 28.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 16(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 16(b): no later than fourteen (14) days before trial,
/// the defense makes its Rule 16(b) case-in-chief material available.
deadline defense-disclosure: 14.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 16(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 16(b)(1), (2): no later than twenty-one (21) days before
/// trial, the defense files and serves any notice of an insanity or other
/// mental-condition defense under FRCrimP 12.2 and of a public-authority
/// defense under FRCrimP 12.3.
deadline defense-notices: 21.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 16(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 23(d): each party files and serves any trial brief no
/// later than seven (7) days before trial or as ordered by the presiding
/// judge.
deadline trial-brief: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 23(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 24(a): each party files and serves any suggested voir
/// dire questions no later than seven (7) days before trial.
deadline voir-dire-questions: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 24(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 30(a): each party files and serves proposed jury
/// instructions no later than seven (7) days before trial; unanticipated
/// instructions may be filed during trial.
deadline jury-instructions: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 30(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 58(g)(2)(E): the appellant's brief is filed and served
/// within twenty-eight (28) days after the filing of the notice of appeal.
deadline magistrate-appeal-appellant-brief: 28.days after MagistrateAppealNoticed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 58(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 58(g)(2)(E): the appellee's responsive brief is filed
/// and served within fourteen (14) days thereafter.
deadline magistrate-appeal-appellee-brief: 14.days after AppellantBriefServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 58(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Wash. LCrR 58(g)(2)(E): the appellant may file and serve a reply
/// brief within seven (7) days thereafter.
deadline magistrate-appeal-reply-brief: 7.days after AppelleeBriefServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Wash. LCrR 58(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
